{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"polarized-servile-jenny","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nCurrent recovery handles interrupted creates but not the retired-first/live-replace crash state where one exact identity remains both live and tombstoned. Recovery must never guess across mismatched identities.\n\n## Outcome\nExtract create recovery and add a pure interrupted-retirement classifier plus repository-backed completion operation behind the `BindingStore` facade. Do not invoke it automatically yet.\n\n## Plan\n1. Move keyed/keyless create recovery into `binding_recovery.py` without changing labels, immutable known-key behavior, three-miss plus 3600-second grace, failure tally, or continue behavior.\n2. Build real fault-cut fixtures for a tombstone persisted before live replacement fails.\n3. Classify retirement completion only when tombstone, forward entry, and reverse entry agree on exact local id and Jira key.\n4. Complete by removing the redundant live forward/reverse pair while retaining the tombstone; repeat is a no-op. Mismatch, corruption, or replace failure safety-aborts and retains evidence.\n\n## Testing\nUse fresh store reloads, identity-mismatch tables, replacement cuts, and keyed/keyless create-recovery regressions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exact tombstone/forward/reverse overlap completes to coherent retired-only bytes while retaining the tombstone.\n- [ ] Repeating completion performs no write.\n- [ ] Any identity mismatch, corrupt live file, or replace failure retains evidence and returns a typed safety abort.\n- [ ] Keyed pending recovery performs no search.\n- [ ] Keyless pending recovery still requires both three misses and 3600 seconds, and one entry failure does not stop others.\n\n## Out of scope\nAutomatic invocation boundary, rich-emission caller cutover, and ADR finalization.","id":"c4f7-82ff-1004-4da5","parent_id":"486a-69ef-6370-48ff","priority":1,"tags":["rp02","binding-recovery","tdd"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-02 S3 T1 — Classify and complete interrupted binding operations"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787027651760140001,"uuid":"05c227df-11ac-4be5-99e5-f1afa187411d"}